WEBVTT

00:01:00.403 --> 00:01:06.117
Five, four, three two, one.

00:01:06.284 --> 00:01:07.744
Ready or not, here I come.

00:02:22.861 --> 00:02:24.446
Hey, Dad?

00:02:25.905 --> 00:02:27.657
Dad.

00:03:30.887 --> 00:03:33.974
You'll stay with Aunt May and
Uncle Ben for a little while.

00:03:34.265 --> 00:03:36.309
- I wanna go with you.
- No.

00:03:40.855 --> 00:03:43.019
Doesn't like crust on
his sandwiches and

00:03:43.021 --> 00:03:45.236
he likes to sleep with
a little light on.

00:03:45.402 --> 00:03:47.529
- Mary. Come on, come on.
- Oh, God.

00:03:51.783 --> 00:03:53.243
Dad.

00:03:54.119 --> 00:03:55.787
Be good.

00:04:13.722 --> 00:04:14.722
Sorry.

00:04:14.806 --> 00:04:16.391
Morning, Flash.

00:04:19.352 --> 00:04:21.438
Good morning, Parker.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.779
Hey. It's Peter, right?

00:04:31.531 --> 00:04:33.033
I really like your photos.

00:04:33.199 --> 00:04:34.826
Oh, thanks. Thanks.

00:04:35.076 --> 00:04:37.454
Listen are you busy Friday night?

00:04:43.001 --> 00:04:45.962
Cool. Can you take pictures
of my boyfriend's car?

00:04:46.129 --> 00:04:49.382
You know, I really wanna frame
a good one for his birthday.

00:04:49.507 --> 00:04:52.636
That's really nice of you. Wow,
that's such a nice thought.

00:04:53.219 --> 00:04:55.138
Yeah, I'll have a
look at the old...

00:04:55.305 --> 00:04:57.057
- The old schedule.
- Okay.

00:04:58.224 --> 00:04:59.997
- Parker.
- Yes, sir?

00:04:59.998 --> 00:05:01.561
You want to keep that skateboard?

00:05:01.728 --> 00:05:03.229
- Yeah.
- Keep it off the ground.

00:05:03.396 --> 00:05:04.731
- Sure. Yeah.
- Wheels up.

00:05:04.898 --> 00:05:06.024
Like that?

00:05:06.191 --> 00:05:07.901
- That's it.
- Okay.

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:12.169
♪ Is there no way down from this ♪

00:05:12.869 --> 00:05:15.076
♪ Peak to solid ground ♪

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:19.715
♪ Without having our ♪

00:05:19.877 --> 00:05:22.517
♪ Gold teeth pulled
from our mouths ♪

00:05:34.094 --> 00:05:35.428
Eat it. Eat it. Eat it.

00:05:35.595 --> 00:05:36.972
Eat it. Eat it.

00:05:37.138 --> 00:05:39.683
Eat it. Eat it. Eat it.

00:05:39.849 --> 00:05:42.268
Eat your vegetables,
Gordon. Come on.

00:05:42.435 --> 00:05:43.895
Come on.

00:05:44.062 --> 00:05:45.230
Hey, Parker, come on.

00:05:45.397 --> 00:05:46.773
Get a picture of this.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:50.110
No, I'm not gonna take a picture
of it. Put him down, man.

00:05:50.276 --> 00:05:52.237
- Come on.
- Gordon, don't eat it.

00:05:52.404 --> 00:05:53.446
Take the picture.

00:05:53.613 --> 00:05:55.073
Put him down, Flash.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:56.825
Take the picture.

00:05:56.992 --> 00:05:59.577
Put him down, Eugene.

00:06:02.622 --> 00:06:03.957
Hey, man.

00:06:05.625 --> 00:06:06.625
Come on.

00:06:06.626 --> 00:06:07.626
Get up, Parker.

00:06:09.879 --> 00:06:10.879
Get up.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.507
Come on. Come on.

00:06:12.674 --> 00:06:13.674
Get up.

00:06:16.303 --> 00:06:17.637
Still not taking the picture.

00:06:18.138 --> 00:06:19.472
Stay down, Parker.

00:06:19.973 --> 00:06:21.474
Who wants one more?

00:06:21.641 --> 00:06:23.226
- One more.
- Flash.

00:06:23.727 --> 00:06:27.147
Flash we still on for
after school today?

00:06:27.314 --> 00:06:28.440
My house, 3:30?

00:06:28.606 --> 00:06:29.816
I hope you did homework.

00:06:29.983 --> 00:06:33.278
Last time, I was
disappointed in you.

00:06:33.445 --> 00:06:35.530
- Okay, move.
- No, how about we go to class?

00:06:35.697 --> 00:06:36.906
How about it?

00:06:39.743 --> 00:06:41.286
Whatever.

00:07:06.394 --> 00:07:08.271
I thought that was
great what you did.

00:07:09.397 --> 00:07:12.066
It was stupid but it was great.

00:07:12.942 --> 00:07:15.820
You should go to the nurse.
You might have a concussion.

00:07:17.906 --> 00:07:18.906
What's your name?

00:07:19.449 --> 00:07:20.533
You don't know my name?

00:07:20.867 --> 00:07:22.702
No, I know your name.

00:07:22.911 --> 00:07:24.579
I want to know if
you know your name.

00:07:26.331 --> 00:07:27.874
Peter.

00:07:28.875 --> 00:07:31.127
- Parker. Peter Parker.
- Okay. Okay, good.

00:07:38.593 --> 00:07:40.387
I'd still go to the nurse though.

00:07:40.553 --> 00:07:41.805
You're Gwen, right?

00:07:41.972 --> 00:07:43.181
Gwen Stacy.

00:07:43.556 --> 00:07:45.183
All right.

00:07:46.434 --> 00:07:48.103
Hey.

00:07:48.269 --> 00:07:51.064
I'm making spaghetti
and meatballs tonight.

00:07:51.648 --> 00:07:53.900
You're serious? Spaghetti
and meatballs.

00:07:54.067 --> 00:07:57.779
Since when don't you like
spaghetti and meatballs, huh?

00:07:58.238 --> 00:07:59.990
- Oh, my God.
- What's up?

00:08:00.156 --> 00:08:01.700
What happened to your face?

00:08:01.866 --> 00:08:04.244
I'm all right. Just,
I fell, skating.

00:08:04.577 --> 00:08:05.996
It's all right.

00:08:06.788 --> 00:08:08.707
Ben Parker, don't you even

00:08:08.873 --> 00:08:11.835
think about leaving that
filthy box in my kitchen.

00:08:12.002 --> 00:08:13.044
My bowling trophies.

00:08:13.211 --> 00:08:16.423
Oh, well, then, by all means
leave that box in my kitchen.

00:08:16.589 --> 00:08:18.049
- What happened to you?
- He fell.

00:08:18.216 --> 00:08:21.011
Why you kids ride those
things, I'll never know.

00:08:21.177 --> 00:08:22.762
Because it's stupid and dangerous.

00:08:22.929 --> 00:08:24.556
Remember when we were stupid?

00:08:24.723 --> 00:08:25.724
No.

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:28.018
- Trust me, we were.
- All right. Good to know.

00:08:28.184 --> 00:08:29.184
Where's the flood?

00:08:29.269 --> 00:08:30.770
Follow me. I'll show you.

00:08:30.937 --> 00:08:32.147
- You serious?
- Yes.

00:08:32.814 --> 00:08:33.940
All right.

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:36.900
It's the condenser tray.

00:08:37.444 --> 00:08:40.530
Too much water for the condenser
tray or the heat exchange tubing.

00:08:40.697 --> 00:08:42.615
This has got to be the fill line.

00:08:42.782 --> 00:08:45.160
That's the only thing
that makes any sense.

00:08:45.327 --> 00:08:46.661
Can you fix it?

00:08:47.245 --> 00:08:50.081
No, not tonight. I'll go by
the hardware store tomorrow.

00:08:50.248 --> 00:08:52.667
Good deal. And meanwhile,
put this on your face.

00:08:54.627 --> 00:08:56.379
How's the other guy look?

00:08:57.964 --> 00:09:01.092
Come on. I know a right
cross when I see one.

00:09:02.218 --> 00:09:05.055
Yes or no? Do I have to
call somebody's father?

00:09:05.597 --> 00:09:06.597
No, no.

00:09:06.681 --> 00:09:07.766
All right.

00:09:07.932 --> 00:09:10.018
Well, I wouldn't
tell your Aunt May.

00:09:10.602 --> 00:09:13.480
I pity the poor kid who'd
have to suffer her wrath.

00:09:15.106 --> 00:09:18.714
Before you come up, see if there's
anything else worth saving.

00:09:18.715 --> 00:09:19.715
Okay.

00:09:36.336 --> 00:09:38.463
- Plumbers don't fix appliances.
- Yes, they do.

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:40.215
They fix pipes and pump things.

00:09:40.382 --> 00:09:42.217
If you ask them to...

00:09:46.513 --> 00:09:49.182
I forgot all about that thing.

00:09:49.349 --> 00:09:50.349
It was your dad's.

00:09:50.392 --> 00:09:52.227
- Yeah.
- He asked us to keep it safe.

00:09:56.272 --> 00:09:59.651
He saw it in the window of that
leather shop over on 9th Avenue.

00:10:00.318 --> 00:10:03.488
He was 19. What does a 19-year-old
kid need with a briefcase?

00:10:03.905 --> 00:10:05.448
And guess who sold it to him.

00:10:05.615 --> 00:10:07.283
- I don't know.
- Your mother.

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:08.535
That's how they met.

00:10:09.577 --> 00:10:12.622
He asked you to keep this safe?
There's nothing in here.

00:10:12.789 --> 00:10:14.541
Have you looked?
There's nothing here.

00:10:14.666 --> 00:10:16.835
Your father was a very
secretive man, Peter.

00:10:18.044 --> 00:10:19.504
Yeah, I know.

00:10:25.552 --> 00:10:26.552
Who's that?

00:10:26.678 --> 00:10:28.221
Do you know who that is?

00:10:28.346 --> 00:10:31.016
Some guy who worked
with your dad, I guess.

00:10:35.895 --> 00:10:37.814
Just take this off the
table, all right?

00:10:37.981 --> 00:10:41.026
We're gonna eat. Off.
And wash your hands.

00:10:41.192 --> 00:10:43.069
- Now.
- All right.

00:10:43.236 --> 00:10:44.237
Go on.

00:11:20.065 --> 00:11:21.483
I need you to be a good boy.

00:11:21.650 --> 00:11:22.776
Where are you going?

00:11:22.942 --> 00:11:26.279
There's something your
mum and I have to do.

00:12:23.378 --> 00:12:24.671
What is this?

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:29.801
"Zero, zero, decay
rate algorithm."

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:34.222
Yeah, one sec, one sec.

00:12:42.230 --> 00:12:44.024
Come in.

00:12:44.691 --> 00:12:45.691
You okay?

00:12:45.692 --> 00:12:48.028
- Yeah. What's up?
- Oh, my God.

00:12:48.194 --> 00:12:49.487
You look just like him.

00:12:50.363 --> 00:12:52.449
- Can I come in?
- Yeah.

00:12:56.870 --> 00:13:00.415
Listen I don't have
much education.

00:13:00.582 --> 00:13:02.042
You know that, Peter.

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:04.096
Hell, I stopped being able to help

00:13:04.097 --> 00:13:05.879
with your homework
when you were 10.

00:13:06.171 --> 00:13:08.631
What I'm trying to say is,

00:13:09.174 --> 00:13:11.551
I know it's been rough for
you without your dad.

00:13:12.010 --> 00:13:13.887
And I know we don't
talk much about them.

00:13:14.054 --> 00:13:17.515
- Yeah, it's all right.
- No, it is not all right.

00:13:18.516 --> 00:13:21.186
I wish I could change
it, but I can't.

00:13:23.063 --> 00:13:24.439
Curt Connors.

00:13:25.065 --> 00:13:27.859
That's the name of the guy in
the picture with your dad.

00:13:28.026 --> 00:13:30.362
They worked together for
years and they were close.

00:13:30.528 --> 00:13:32.906
But after that night,
we never saw him again.

00:13:33.531 --> 00:13:35.033
He never even called.

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:36.409
Not once.

00:13:38.912 --> 00:13:40.538
Go figure.

00:13:44.417 --> 00:13:45.417
She's pretty.

00:13:50.548 --> 00:13:51.591
Uncle Ben.

00:13:51.758 --> 00:13:53.009
What?

00:13:53.593 --> 00:13:55.095
You're a pretty great dad.

00:14:51.151 --> 00:14:52.444
Excuse me.

00:14:52.610 --> 00:14:53.610
What?

00:14:53.611 --> 00:14:55.155
Can I help you?

00:14:55.322 --> 00:14:57.594
I don't know. I'm here
to see Dr Connors.

00:14:57.595 --> 00:14:58.595
Right.

00:14:58.783 --> 00:15:00.660
You'll find yourself to the left.

00:15:02.495 --> 00:15:04.247
You are here for the internship?

00:15:05.206 --> 00:15:06.499
Yeah. Yeah.

00:15:06.666 --> 00:15:07.751
Okay.

00:15:07.917 --> 00:15:09.794
You'll find your
badge to the left.

00:15:15.383 --> 00:15:16.676
Having trouble finding yourself?

00:15:17.427 --> 00:15:18.427
No. Yeah, I got it.

00:15:20.847 --> 00:15:21.847
Okay...

00:15:21.848 --> 00:15:23.725
Mr Guevara.

00:15:24.989 --> 00:15:25.989
Thanks.

00:15:26.853 --> 00:15:28.980
Welcome to Oscorp.

00:15:29.147 --> 00:15:31.983
Born from the mind of our
founder, Norman Osborn,

00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:35.820
the Oscorp Tower houses
108 floors of innovation.

00:15:36.946 --> 00:15:38.969
Our scientific minds
are pushing the

00:15:38.970 --> 00:15:40.992
boundaries of defence, biomedical,

00:15:41.159 --> 00:15:43.953
and chemical technologies.
The future lies within.

00:15:44.329 --> 00:15:45.413
Welcome to Oscorp.

00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:48.040
I'm Gwen Stacy, a senior
at Midtown Science,

00:15:48.083 --> 00:15:49.501
and head intern to Dr Connors.

00:15:49.668 --> 00:15:51.836
I'll be with you for the
duration of your visit.

00:15:52.379 --> 00:15:53.672
Where I go, you go.

00:15:53.838 --> 00:15:56.142
That's the rule. Remember
that all will be fine.

00:15:56.143 --> 00:15:57.143
Come on.

00:15:57.342 --> 00:15:58.718
- If you forget that...
- Listen.

00:15:58.885 --> 00:15:59.885
Look, listen.

00:15:59.970 --> 00:16:01.554
Tell them Rodrigo Guevara is here.

00:16:01.721 --> 00:16:04.015
Just tell them Rodrigo
Guevara is here.

00:16:04.182 --> 00:16:05.350
My name's Rodrigo.

00:16:05.517 --> 00:16:08.353
I guess I don't need to tell you
what happens if you forget.

00:16:09.229 --> 00:16:10.229
Shall we?

00:16:17.904 --> 00:16:19.531
Come around this way.

00:16:23.743 --> 00:16:24.911
Good afternoon, Gwen.

00:16:25.078 --> 00:16:26.078
Dr Connors.

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:28.080
Welcome.

00:16:28.123 --> 00:16:30.917
My name is Dr Curtis Connors.

00:16:31.084 --> 00:16:33.336
Yes, in case you're
wondering, I'm a southpaw.

00:16:33.503 --> 00:16:34.754
I'm not a cripple,

00:16:34.921 --> 00:16:38.258
I'm a scientist, and the world's
foremost authority on herpetology.

00:16:38.425 --> 00:16:41.177
That's reptiles, for those
of you who don't know.

00:16:41.344 --> 00:16:45.682
Like the Parkinson's patient who
watches on in horror as her

00:16:45.849 --> 00:16:49.269
body slowly betrays her, or the
man with macular degeneration

00:16:49.436 --> 00:16:53.273
whose eyes grow dimmer each
day, I long to fix myself.

00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:57.277
I want to create a world
without weakness.

00:16:57.444 --> 00:17:00.405
Anyone care to venture
a guess just how?

00:17:00.905 --> 00:17:01.905
Yes.

00:17:01.948 --> 00:17:02.948
Stem cells?

00:17:03.074 --> 00:17:04.659
Promising. But the solution

00:17:04.826 --> 00:17:07.620
I'm thinking of is more radical.

00:17:09.914 --> 00:17:11.458
- No one?
- Cross-species genetics.

00:17:19.716 --> 00:17:20.925
Person gets Parkinson's,

00:17:21.092 --> 00:17:23.470
when the brain cells
that produce dopamine,

00:17:23.637 --> 00:17:25.639
start to disappear.

00:17:25.805 --> 00:17:29.851
But a zebra fish has the ability
to regenerate cells on command.

00:17:30.310 --> 00:17:31.936
If you could give this ability

00:17:32.103 --> 00:17:34.981
to the woman you're talking
about, that's that. She's...

00:17:36.024 --> 00:17:37.359
She's curing herself.

00:17:37.859 --> 00:17:40.403
Yeah, you just have to look
past the gills on her neck.

00:17:43.990 --> 00:17:45.158
And you are?

00:17:47.327 --> 00:17:49.204
He's one of Midtown Science's

00:17:49.371 --> 00:17:50.872
- best and brightest.
- Really?

00:17:51.039 --> 00:17:52.040
Second in his class.

00:17:53.124 --> 00:17:55.001
- Second?
- Yeah.

00:17:55.168 --> 00:17:56.168
Sure about that?

00:17:56.169 --> 00:17:57.629
I'm pretty sure.

00:18:01.132 --> 00:18:03.025
I'm afraid duty calls.
I'll leave you in

00:18:03.026 --> 00:18:05.011
the more-than-capable
hands of Miss Stacy.

00:18:05.345 --> 00:18:07.055
Nice meeting you all.

00:18:10.183 --> 00:18:11.685
If you'd like to gather round.

00:18:11.851 --> 00:18:13.853
Welcome to Oscorp's tree of life.

00:18:14.688 --> 00:18:17.440
Our planet's tree
of life is immense.

00:18:18.066 --> 00:18:19.150
At Oscorp's

00:18:19.317 --> 00:18:21.027
- Cross-Species Division...
- Hi.

00:18:21.194 --> 00:18:24.197
We endeavour to explore
exciting new methods...

00:18:25.615 --> 00:18:26.825
What are you doing, "Rodrigo"?

00:18:29.869 --> 00:18:31.121
Oh, yeah.

00:18:31.287 --> 00:18:32.539
What are you doing here?

00:18:32.706 --> 00:18:33.873
I work here. I don't.

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:35.625
I was gonna say I work here,

00:18:35.792 --> 00:18:39.004
but it seems like you do work
here. So you know that I don't.

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:40.170
You following me?

00:18:40.213 --> 00:18:43.341
No, I'm not following you, no.
I had no idea you worked here.

00:18:43.508 --> 00:18:44.718
Why would you be here?

00:18:44.884 --> 00:18:48.305
I just snuck in because
I love science.

00:18:48.471 --> 00:18:50.265
- You love it.
- I'm passionate about it.

00:18:50.432 --> 00:18:52.058
So you snuck in?

00:18:52.225 --> 00:18:54.394
- I have to lead this tour group.
- I know.

00:18:54.561 --> 00:18:57.480
I'll ask you more about this
later. Do not get me in trouble.

00:18:57.647 --> 00:18:59.899
- I promise you I won't.
- Stay with the group.

00:19:00.567 --> 00:19:04.029
All right, guys? I'm gonna take
you to the bioreactor room now.

00:19:07.824 --> 00:19:09.326
Sorry. Yo.

00:19:10.744 --> 00:19:11.828
Sorry.

00:21:35.221 --> 00:21:38.850
We received the results from the
mRNA sequences this morning.

00:21:39.017 --> 00:21:41.811
They were disappointing.

00:21:47.567 --> 00:21:48.735
Define "disappointing."

00:21:48.902 --> 00:21:50.236
Another dead end.

00:21:50.403 --> 00:21:52.072
It's the decay rate algorithm.

00:21:52.530 --> 00:21:54.741
- And this is to be expected.
- Expected?

00:21:54.908 --> 00:21:56.242
You said you were close.

00:21:56.409 --> 00:21:58.578
We are close, but
it's gonna take time.

00:21:58.745 --> 00:21:59.954
He doesn't have time.

00:22:00.121 --> 00:22:02.415
Norman Osborn is
dying, Dr Connors.

00:22:02.957 --> 00:22:04.209
Save him.

00:22:06.503 --> 00:22:08.380
Or we'll both lose our heads.

00:22:26.773 --> 00:22:28.233
All right, give me the badge.

00:22:30.443 --> 00:22:31.778
Give it to me.

00:22:35.448 --> 00:22:36.825
Sorry.

00:23:37.719 --> 00:23:40.096
Disgusting. Now I smell like beer.

00:23:41.681 --> 00:23:42.849
I didn't mean to do that.

00:23:43.016 --> 00:23:46.353
I didn't mean to, I
didn't... I didn't...

00:23:47.687 --> 00:23:48.855
Get your hand off her.

00:23:49.022 --> 00:23:50.690
I'm trying to get my...

00:23:54.361 --> 00:23:55.361
Are you kidding?

00:23:55.445 --> 00:23:56.445
I'm sorry.

00:23:56.446 --> 00:23:57.614
Are you kidding me?

00:23:58.198 --> 00:23:59.908
- Hey, get him, Rudy.
- Hey.

00:24:03.203 --> 00:24:04.371
Man, I'm sorry.

00:24:04.537 --> 00:24:05.622
Man, are you all right?

00:24:08.541 --> 00:24:10.085
- Take him down.
- Come on.

