01:07:14.502 --> 01:07:16.129
Just drive.

01:07:16.713 --> 01:07:17.922
Okay.

01:07:24.179 --> 01:07:25.680
You're having trouble there?

01:07:25.847 --> 01:07:27.515
The head goes on the other...

01:07:27.682 --> 01:07:29.225
Help Gwen's friend with his fish.

01:07:29.392 --> 01:07:30.602
On, I...

01:07:30.769 --> 01:07:31.853
I got no idea.

01:07:32.020 --> 01:07:33.563
First time.

01:07:33.730 --> 01:07:35.315
- Branzino.
- George.

01:07:35.482 --> 01:07:36.574
Tell us about your day.

01:07:36.575 --> 01:07:38.234
Did you catch that spider guy yet?

01:07:38.401 --> 01:07:39.986
No, we didn't catch him yet.

01:07:40.153 --> 01:07:42.030
But we will. He's an amateur

01:07:42.197 --> 01:07:44.908
who's assaulting civilians
in the dead of night.

01:07:45.075 --> 01:07:48.495
He's clumsy, he leaves clues,
but he's still dangerous.

01:07:49.371 --> 01:07:50.830
He's assaulting people?

01:07:52.666 --> 01:07:53.667
I'm not sure.

01:07:53.833 --> 01:07:57.420
I mean, I saw that video, with
him and the car thief, and

01:07:57.587 --> 01:08:00.715
I think most people
would say that he was

01:08:01.466 --> 01:08:02.842
providing a public service.

01:08:03.551 --> 01:08:05.512
Most people would be wrong.

01:08:06.805 --> 01:08:08.348
If I wanted the car thief off the

01:08:08.349 --> 01:08:10.266
street, he'd already
be off the street.

01:08:10.433 --> 01:08:11.685
So why wasn't he then?

01:08:15.689 --> 01:08:16.731
Let me illuminate you.

01:08:16.898 --> 01:08:19.526
The car thief was leading
us to the people who run

01:08:19.693 --> 01:08:21.903
the operation. It's a
six-month-long sting.

01:08:22.070 --> 01:08:25.073
It's called strategy. I'm sure
you're aware of the term?

01:08:25.240 --> 01:08:27.117
You've heard about that in school?

01:08:27.118 --> 01:08:28.909
- Yeah.
- Good.

01:08:28.952 --> 01:08:30.203
I know.

01:08:30.370 --> 01:08:33.039
- He didn't know you had a plan.
- You seem to know

01:08:33.206 --> 01:08:34.958
a lot about this. Know
something we don't?

01:08:35.125 --> 01:08:37.419
- Whose side are you on?
- I'm not on anyone's side.

01:08:37.585 --> 01:08:38.962
I saw a video on the internet...

01:08:39.129 --> 01:08:40.672
You saw the video on the internet.

01:08:40.839 --> 01:08:43.049
- Well, then the case is closed.
- Well, no.

01:08:43.216 --> 01:08:44.216
If you watch the video...

01:08:44.342 --> 01:08:45.802
Maybe send you a link?

01:08:45.969 --> 01:08:47.637
It looks like he's trying to help.

01:08:47.804 --> 01:08:50.682
On the internet he's being
made out to look like a hero.

01:08:50.849 --> 01:08:51.849
No, no.

01:08:51.850 --> 01:08:53.393
I'm not saying he's a hero.

01:08:53.560 --> 01:08:55.895
- What are you trying to say?
- He's trying to help.

01:08:56.062 --> 01:08:57.529
He's trying to do something
the police can't.

01:08:57.564 --> 01:08:58.940
Something the police can't?

01:08:59.107 --> 01:09:00.650
- I don't know.
- What do you think we do?

01:09:00.817 --> 01:09:02.360
Sit around eating doughnuts

01:09:02.527 --> 01:09:04.321
with our thumbs
planted up our asses?

01:09:04.487 --> 01:09:06.531
- George. George.
- Daddy.

01:09:06.640 --> 01:09:07.640
- Up your what?
- Howard.

01:09:07.641 --> 01:09:09.451
He stands for what you stand for.

01:09:09.617 --> 01:09:11.161
Protecting innocent
people from bad guys.

01:09:11.328 --> 01:09:13.413
I stand for law and order.
That's what I stand for.

01:09:13.580 --> 01:09:15.165
Okay? I wear a badge.

01:09:15.332 --> 01:09:18.376
This guy wears a
mask like an outlaw.

01:09:18.543 --> 01:09:21.087
He's hunting down criminals
that all look the same,

01:09:21.254 --> 01:09:23.423
like he's got some sort
of personal vendetta.

01:09:23.590 --> 01:09:26.593
But he's not protecting
innocent people, Mr Parker.

01:09:26.760 --> 01:09:28.595
Let's get some air, Peter.

01:09:29.220 --> 01:09:31.389
- Dad, we need to talk.
- Yes, we do.

01:09:33.767 --> 01:09:35.602
Thank you for having me. I'm sorry

01:09:35.769 --> 01:09:38.021
if I insulted you. It
was not my intention.

01:09:38.229 --> 01:09:39.247
You're welcome.

01:09:39.248 --> 01:09:41.524
Branzino was real good, Mrs Stacy.

01:09:41.691 --> 01:09:43.777
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

01:09:45.487 --> 01:09:48.031
- Dad.
- Yeah?

01:09:54.788 --> 01:09:56.706
Well, that was something.

01:09:58.166 --> 01:10:01.252
I'm sorry. I thought he was going
to arrest me at one point.

01:10:01.419 --> 01:10:04.047
No, I wouldn't have
let him arrest you

01:10:08.802 --> 01:10:11.513
- What happened to your face?
- I wanna tell you something.

01:10:13.390 --> 01:10:14.641
Okay.

01:10:19.771 --> 01:10:21.064
I've been bitten...

01:10:25.360 --> 01:10:26.360
So have I.

01:10:31.741 --> 01:10:33.159
Okay.

01:10:34.661 --> 01:10:37.163
Okay, okay, okay. I gotta
tell you this one thing.

01:10:37.330 --> 01:10:39.082
I gotta tell you this thing about

01:10:39.249 --> 01:10:42.085
- the vigilante and the car thief.
- Oh, okay.

01:10:42.252 --> 01:10:43.920
What?

01:10:44.087 --> 01:10:46.339
- No, no, no.
- I don't want to talk about that.

01:10:46.506 --> 01:10:48.174
Forget that. I won't
talk about that.

01:10:48.341 --> 01:10:50.593
- I'm gonna talk about me, okay?
- What about you?

01:10:50.760 --> 01:10:54.597
It's impo... I wish
I could just...

01:10:54.764 --> 01:10:56.016
I can't. It's hard to say.

01:10:56.182 --> 01:10:57.183
Just say it.

01:10:57.350 --> 01:10:59.477
- I don't know.
- Say it.

01:11:02.314 --> 01:11:03.606
What? What?

01:11:07.068 --> 01:11:08.778
What?

01:11:12.824 --> 01:11:14.701
Okay, then forget it.

01:11:22.834 --> 01:11:24.294
You?

01:11:32.927 --> 01:11:35.055
- You're Spider-Man.
- Shut up.

01:11:40.060 --> 01:11:41.561
Gwen?

01:11:42.812 --> 01:11:44.147
Gwen...

01:11:45.190 --> 01:11:47.108
Your father wants
you to come inside.

01:11:47.525 --> 01:11:48.735
Okay.

01:11:48.902 --> 01:11:49.903
- Okay?
- Yeah.

01:11:52.697 --> 01:11:53.740
Gwen.

01:11:53.865 --> 01:11:55.575
I'm coming.

01:12:27.065 --> 01:12:28.858
Oh, I'm in trouble.

01:12:52.340 --> 01:12:55.302
Will you please find out
what is going on, Alfred?

01:13:02.726 --> 01:13:03.726
Excellent.

01:13:06.896 --> 01:13:07.897
Hey.

01:13:10.692 --> 01:13:12.027
Hey. What is that?

01:13:12.152 --> 01:13:14.070
- Oh, my God.
- I don't know.

01:13:14.195 --> 01:13:15.655
Get back in the car.

01:13:20.744 --> 01:13:22.120
Help.

01:13:23.830 --> 01:13:24.830
Help.

01:14:04.829 --> 01:14:07.040
Incoming.

01:14:28.019 --> 01:14:29.019
Somebody help.

01:14:29.562 --> 01:14:31.231
Help me. My kid is trapped.

01:14:40.991 --> 01:14:42.158
I want my dad.

01:14:42.492 --> 01:14:43.535
Dad.

01:14:43.702 --> 01:14:45.078
- Hey, hey, hey.
- Help.

01:14:45.245 --> 01:14:47.247
- Hey buddy. It's okay.
- Get away.

01:14:48.206 --> 01:14:49.332
- Help.
- Hey, look.

01:14:50.875 --> 01:14:52.752
Just a normal guy, all right?

01:14:54.462 --> 01:14:55.462
Wanna hold this?

01:14:57.048 --> 01:14:58.048
Hold my mask.

01:14:58.425 --> 01:14:59.425
All right.

01:15:00.927 --> 01:15:02.387
What's your name?

01:15:02.554 --> 01:15:03.554
Jack?

01:15:04.264 --> 01:15:05.932
- Yes.
- Let's get you out of here.

01:15:07.309 --> 01:15:09.060
Okay, stay very still.

01:15:09.127 --> 01:15:10.127
All right.

01:15:10.228 --> 01:15:11.479
Okay, I got you.

01:15:15.734 --> 01:15:16.734
Okay, look.

01:15:16.735 --> 01:15:18.361
I'll undo the belt. You hold on

01:15:18.528 --> 01:15:20.572
to that seat in front
of you. On three?

01:15:20.822 --> 01:15:23.491
- All right.
- Okay, one, two, three.

01:15:25.618 --> 01:15:27.787
See how easy that was?
You did a great job.

01:15:27.954 --> 01:15:29.664
All right, okay.

01:15:43.261 --> 01:15:44.638
Jack, climb now.

01:15:44.804 --> 01:15:46.431
- I can't.
- Yes, you can.

01:15:51.811 --> 01:15:53.813
Put it on, the mask.

01:15:53.980 --> 01:15:55.398
It's gonna make you strong.

01:15:55.982 --> 01:15:57.317
Jack, trust me.

01:15:57.484 --> 01:15:58.484
Put it on.

01:15:59.235 --> 01:16:01.863
There you go. That's
it. That's it, buddy.

01:16:02.030 --> 01:16:03.156
Okay, now, climb.

01:16:03.323 --> 01:16:04.324
Come on, Jack.

01:16:07.911 --> 01:16:08.911
Do me a favour.

01:16:08.912 --> 01:16:10.413
A little faster, okay, bud?

01:16:10.664 --> 01:16:12.999
You're doing great, buddy.
You're doing great.

01:16:13.166 --> 01:16:14.250
That's it. Keep coming.

01:16:14.417 --> 01:16:15.835
Keep it coming.

01:16:16.002 --> 01:16:17.045
Keep coming.

01:16:17.962 --> 01:16:19.297
No.

01:16:33.937 --> 01:16:35.647
Jack. Oh, God.

01:16:35.814 --> 01:16:37.315
Thank God.

01:16:39.025 --> 01:16:40.360
You okay?

01:16:43.405 --> 01:16:44.864
My son. My son.

01:16:45.699 --> 01:16:46.825
Oh, my son.

01:16:46.950 --> 01:16:48.743
My son.

01:16:53.206 --> 01:16:54.290
Who are you?

01:16:56.710 --> 01:16:58.211
Spider-Man.

01:17:45.258 --> 01:17:47.260
Beautiful.

01:17:55.435 --> 01:17:56.478
Settle down, guys.

01:17:57.479 --> 01:17:59.105
Settle down, boys. Settle down.

01:17:59.272 --> 01:18:01.441
- Come on.
- Listen. At approximately

01:18:01.608 --> 01:18:03.388
9 p.m. last night,
an incident took

01:18:03.389 --> 01:18:05.070
place on the Williamsburg Bridge.

01:18:05.612 --> 01:18:07.447
Much of what occurred
is speculation

01:18:07.614 --> 01:18:10.408
at this point. However,
several eyewitnesses

01:18:10.575 --> 01:18:13.995
to the crime, as well as our
own preliminary findings, have

01:18:14.162 --> 01:18:17.123
positively placed one
individual at the scene.

01:18:17.290 --> 01:18:20.335
Which is why, this morning,
I am issuing a warrant

01:18:20.502 --> 01:18:23.838
for the masked vigilante
known as Spider-Man.

01:18:29.761 --> 01:18:31.522
And lastly, city
council members met

01:18:31.523 --> 01:18:33.473
with homeowners and
airport officials,

01:18:33.640 --> 01:18:35.308
in the first of four meetings...

01:18:42.607 --> 01:18:43.984
It's so beautiful.

01:18:44.150 --> 01:18:45.986
Knows how to bite though.

01:18:46.152 --> 01:18:47.904
Who else knows about this?

01:18:48.071 --> 01:18:49.071
Just you.

01:18:49.114 --> 01:18:50.365
Really?

01:18:52.826 --> 01:18:54.744
Hey, you don't...

01:18:55.495 --> 01:18:58.081
You don't believe what the
police are saying, do you?

01:18:58.957 --> 01:19:00.458
Of course not.

01:19:02.460 --> 01:19:03.837
Does it scare you?

01:19:04.004 --> 01:19:05.839
What you can do?

01:19:08.341 --> 01:19:09.676
No.

01:19:10.760 --> 01:19:11.886
No.

01:19:12.846 --> 01:19:14.973
What did that thing on
the bridge look like?

01:19:15.515 --> 01:19:17.976
It was real big. Too
big to be human.

01:19:18.351 --> 01:19:19.894
You gotta lay low.

01:19:20.687 --> 01:19:22.063
No, can't do that.

01:19:22.230 --> 01:19:23.815
You've got to.

01:19:24.649 --> 01:19:26.151
I mean, why?

01:19:26.443 --> 01:19:28.945
Because of last night.

01:19:29.112 --> 01:19:31.114
Those people on the bridge.

01:19:31.281 --> 01:19:35.285
Whatever was attacking them
would have killed them.

01:19:36.786 --> 01:19:39.456
So I gotta go after it.

01:19:40.957 --> 01:19:42.000
That's not your job.

01:19:43.418 --> 01:19:45.003
Maybe it is.

01:19:49.924 --> 01:19:51.468
I really liked kissing you.

01:19:54.095 --> 01:19:55.597
You're an amazing kisser.

01:19:58.391 --> 01:19:59.559
Well, you know, it was...

01:19:59.726 --> 01:20:01.728
It was good for me too.

01:20:04.397 --> 01:20:06.024
Yeah?

01:20:15.408 --> 01:20:16.576
Who did that?

01:20:38.306 --> 01:20:39.307
Hello.

01:20:48.900 --> 01:20:51.152
It's not nice to snoop.

01:20:54.030 --> 01:20:55.949
I gave everyone the week off.

01:20:58.159 --> 01:20:59.159
Yeah.

01:21:00.120 --> 01:21:01.454
Shouldn't you be at school?

01:21:03.206 --> 01:21:05.250
No, I got a free track.

01:21:05.417 --> 01:21:07.419
I wanted to ask you a question.

01:21:08.128 --> 01:21:10.630
How would a predator
track a reptile?

01:21:10.755 --> 01:21:13.633
Oh, they don't. Most
reptiles are at the top

01:21:13.800 --> 01:21:15.051
of their food chain.

01:21:15.218 --> 01:21:16.720
Kings of their domain.

01:21:16.886 --> 01:21:18.388
They gotta have vulnerabilities.

01:21:18.555 --> 01:21:21.099
Why the sudden interest
in the cold-blooded?

01:21:24.644 --> 01:21:25.937
Just asking a question.

01:21:26.104 --> 01:21:28.940
I got school stuff.

01:21:29.107 --> 01:21:31.109
Biology profiles to do.

01:21:31.526 --> 01:21:33.778
So because of the cold blood,

01:21:33.945 --> 01:21:35.864
would they react to
changes in temperatures?

01:21:36.031 --> 01:21:37.407
You'd have to catch one first.

01:21:38.325 --> 01:21:41.619
Did you know there's a rumour
of a new species in New York?

01:21:41.786 --> 01:21:43.288
Beautiful and quite large.

01:21:44.456 --> 01:21:46.416
What do you know about
it? You seen it?

01:21:46.583 --> 01:21:48.585
No, it's not yet classified.

01:21:51.546 --> 01:21:55.466
But it can be aggressive,
if threatened.

01:22:03.141 --> 01:22:04.392
Doc, you all right?

01:22:04.559 --> 01:22:07.187
Never been better, Peter.
Never been better.

01:22:07.354 --> 01:22:08.897
Now, if you'll excuse me.

01:22:09.064 --> 01:22:11.816
Afraid I have to ask you to
leave. I have a new project

01:22:11.983 --> 01:22:14.402
I'm working on. I
need to be alone.

01:22:15.028 --> 01:22:17.322
Good. Good, good.

01:22:17.864 --> 01:22:19.699
Good.

01:22:20.283 --> 01:22:23.203
Don't worry, Mr
Parker. I'll be back.

01:22:24.204 --> 01:22:26.331
Wonderful things are coming.

01:22:27.582 --> 01:22:29.376
Wonderful things.

01:22:43.932 --> 01:22:45.225
Fred?

01:22:50.021 --> 01:22:52.232
Mr Mayor, if there
was a giant dinosaur

01:22:52.399 --> 01:22:54.901
running around you would
be the first to know.

01:22:55.026 --> 01:22:57.612
So tell your son he can
rest easy, all right?

01:22:57.779 --> 01:23:00.323
Yeah. You and me both, sir.

01:23:00.390 --> 01:23:01.914
Okay. Bye-bye.

01:23:02.816 --> 01:23:05.545
Mr Parker, why are
you not in school?

01:23:05.569 --> 01:23:07.664
- Got a free track.
- Okay, well, I do not.

01:23:07.831 --> 01:23:09.082
So make your point quickly.

01:23:09.249 --> 01:23:11.626
Fine, there may not be a
dinosaur running around.

01:23:11.751 --> 01:23:14.087
There is something more
dangerous, and I know who.

01:23:14.254 --> 01:23:15.839
- You know who?
- Dr Curtis Connors.

01:23:16.006 --> 01:23:17.382
- He's a biochemist.
- Of Oscorp?

01:23:17.549 --> 01:23:19.050
- That's right.
- Dr Connors,

01:23:19.217 --> 01:23:21.219
who's my daughter's
mentor. Is that who?

01:23:21.386 --> 01:23:22.595
- That's the one.
- Okay.

01:23:22.762 --> 01:23:26.057
Recently, Dr Connors gave Gwen
a college recommendation.

01:23:26.224 --> 01:23:28.268
It was beautiful. When
I read it, I cried.

01:23:28.393 --> 01:23:30.603
You would have me believe that he

01:23:30.770 --> 01:23:32.981
is running around dressed
up like a dinosaur?

01:23:33.148 --> 01:23:34.983
Not dressing up and
not a dinosaur. He

01:23:34.984 --> 01:23:36.818
has transformed himself
into a lizard.

01:23:40.071 --> 01:23:41.614
Let me ask you a question.

01:23:41.781 --> 01:23:44.909
Do I look like the
Mayor of Tokyo to you?

01:23:45.035 --> 01:23:47.537
I'm telling you the
absolute truth.

01:23:47.704 --> 01:23:50.749
This man has worked for his whole
life on cross-species genetics.

01:23:50.915 --> 01:23:52.617
He lost an arm, he
tried to grow it

01:23:52.618 --> 01:23:54.461
back, but the equation
was imbalanced.

01:23:54.627 --> 01:23:57.088
He has turned into a lizard.
He's using lizard DNA.

01:23:57.255 --> 01:23:59.111
He is dangerous,
and he is planning

01:23:59.112 --> 01:24:00.967
something horrific.
I know. I know.

01:24:01.134 --> 01:24:03.595
Okay. All right, I get it.

01:24:04.471 --> 01:24:05.513
Here's what we'll do.

01:24:05.972 --> 01:24:08.767
You'll go back to hanging out
with the citizens of Tokyo.

01:24:08.933 --> 01:24:11.144
I'm gonna go back to
protecting the citizens

01:24:11.311 --> 01:24:13.355
of this fine, fair city of ours.

01:24:13.521 --> 01:24:16.793
Sergeant Butler, please escort
Mr Parker back to school.

01:24:16.794 --> 01:24:18.902
Captain Stacy, I'm
not messing around.

01:24:19.069 --> 01:24:22.113
Just bring him in. Just call him
in. You have to call him in.

01:24:22.280 --> 01:24:23.907
He is a danger to everybody.

01:24:24.074 --> 01:24:26.326
- Just, please, listen to me.
- Let's go.

01:24:30.664 --> 01:24:31.998
Jimmy.

01:24:33.208 --> 01:24:36.086
Get me everything we have
on Dr Curtis Connors.

01:24:36.211 --> 01:24:38.797
- Okay? Right away.
- Yeah.

01:25:04.197 --> 01:25:06.157
Subject: Dr Curtis Connors.

01:25:06.324 --> 01:25:07.867
Current temperature: 89.7.

01:25:08.034 --> 01:25:09.494
Steady for 48 hours.

01:25:09.661 --> 01:25:12.163
Blood panels reveal lymphocyte
and monocyte readings,

01:25:12.330 --> 01:25:13.999
consistent with subject's past.

01:25:19.754 --> 01:25:21.423
Clotting rate vastly improved.

01:25:21.589 --> 01:25:24.592
Marked enhancement,
in muscle response,

01:25:24.759 --> 01:25:26.136
strength and elasticity.

01:25:33.977 --> 01:25:36.062
Eyesight similarly improved.

01:25:36.229 --> 01:25:38.732
Subject no longer requires
corrective lenses.

01:25:44.070 --> 01:25:45.989
This is no longer
about curing ills.

01:25:46.531 --> 01:25:49.159
This is about finding perfection.

01:25:58.418 --> 01:26:00.503
In attempt to redress
regenerative relapse,

01:26:00.628 --> 01:26:04.424
dosage has been increased
to 200 milligrams.

01:27:39.227 --> 01:27:40.979
You stopped me once.

01:27:41.813 --> 01:27:44.190
You won't stop me again.

01:27:46.192 --> 01:27:49.195
I'm getting stronger every day.

01:28:27.942 --> 01:28:29.486
Oh, that sucked.

01:28:40.914 --> 01:28:42.582
Peter Parker.

01:29:00.266 --> 01:29:01.810
Come in.

01:29:04.270 --> 01:29:07.607
You should maybe consider
coming in through the lobby.

01:29:09.234 --> 01:29:12.278
Also, my father is
under the impression

01:29:12.404 --> 01:29:14.562
that you require
psychiatric attention.

01:29:14.563 --> 01:29:15.581
Oh, really?

01:29:15.582 --> 01:29:17.117
Peter.

01:29:17.617 --> 01:29:18.660
What happened?

01:29:18.785 --> 01:29:20.161
You should see the other guy.

01:29:21.997 --> 01:29:26.418
The other guy, in this instance,
being a giant mutant lizard.

01:29:26.584 --> 01:29:27.585
Hey, Gwen, honey.

01:29:27.752 --> 01:29:28.752
Do you want cocoa?

01:29:28.837 --> 01:29:29.963
Howard's making some.

01:29:34.551 --> 01:29:35.969
No, Dad, I do not want cocoa.

01:29:36.136 --> 01:29:37.804
Honestly, I'm 17 years old.

01:29:37.871 --> 01:29:38.905
Okay.

01:29:38.972 --> 01:29:41.184
I remembered somebody
saying her fantasy

01:29:41.185 --> 01:29:43.018
was to live in a chocolate house.

01:29:43.184 --> 01:29:44.644
Well, that's impractical.

01:29:44.769 --> 01:29:46.229
And fattening.

01:29:49.482 --> 01:29:50.567
Chocolate house.

01:29:53.445 --> 01:29:55.238
- Sorry, Dad.
- It's good.

01:29:55.405 --> 01:29:58.199
I can't have cocoa right
now because I'm work...

01:29:58.325 --> 01:30:01.453
I'm doing this...

01:30:01.619 --> 01:30:03.246
I have cramps.

01:30:04.122 --> 01:30:06.166
I feel kind of pukey
and just sort of...

01:30:06.333 --> 01:30:08.626
- Like, emotional. I keep crying.
- It's okay. Good.

01:30:08.752 --> 01:30:10.503
- Good.
- It's brutal.

01:30:11.379 --> 01:30:12.714
You don't want to know.

01:30:12.881 --> 01:30:14.049
- It's, like, bad.
- Got it.

01:30:14.215 --> 01:30:16.176
- Thanks, Daddy.
- All right.

01:30:41.284 --> 01:30:43.303
Easy, bug boy

01:30:44.454 --> 01:30:45.872
What'd you call me?

01:30:50.960 --> 01:30:52.796
I'm going to be all right.

01:30:52.962 --> 01:30:55.674
- No. No.
- Yes. Yes.

01:30:57.050 --> 01:30:59.552
I know what this is.

01:30:59.719 --> 01:31:01.054
What is it?

01:31:01.972 --> 01:31:05.141
Every day, for as long as
I can remember, my father

01:31:05.308 --> 01:31:09.004
has left every morning and
he's put a badge on his chest

01:31:09.871 --> 01:31:11.865
and strapped a gun to his hip.

01:31:14.734 --> 01:31:17.112
And every day, for as
long as I can remember.

01:31:17.278 --> 01:31:19.739
I haven't known if he
was gonna make it home.

01:31:29.290 --> 01:31:31.126
I got you.

01:31:32.377 --> 01:31:33.545
Okay?

01:31:36.256 --> 01:31:37.257
Okay?

01:31:38.842 --> 01:31:40.927
I gotta stop him, though.

01:31:41.594 --> 01:31:44.514
I have to, because I created him.

01:31:47.809 --> 01:31:49.269
What do you mean?

01:31:50.687 --> 01:31:52.772
I gave him an equation

01:31:55.317 --> 01:31:57.444
that made all of this possible.

01:32:05.076 --> 01:32:07.954
Something my father had
been working on, you know.

01:32:08.121 --> 01:32:11.124
Secretly. Now I realise
why he kept it a secret.

01:32:13.918 --> 01:32:16.379
Point is, this is
my responsibility.

01:32:19.716 --> 01:32:21.885
I have to fix it.

01:32:24.971 --> 01:32:26.640
Peter.

01:32:27.682 --> 01:32:29.392
Hey.

01:32:32.687 --> 01:32:34.814
Let's get out of here.

01:32:34.981 --> 01:32:36.775
Let's just get out of here.

01:32:36.941 --> 01:32:38.652
Just for a minute. Can we?

01:32:39.361 --> 01:32:41.321
- No. No.
- Yeah. Yes.

01:32:41.488 --> 01:32:42.656
- Yes.
- No.

01:32:42.822 --> 01:32:43.990
Yes.

01:32:44.157 --> 01:32:46.660
If my parents see me
leaving, I'm dead.

01:32:51.247 --> 01:32:53.333
Your parents aren't
gonna see you leaving.

01:33:06.680 --> 01:33:08.306
Peter Parker.

01:33:08.473 --> 01:33:10.141
Spider-Man.

01:33:10.517 --> 01:33:13.728
I'm not the one who needs help.

01:33:13.937 --> 01:33:17.232
There will be no more
loneliness, no more outcasts.

01:33:17.399 --> 01:33:21.152
Species-wide distribution
could enhance

01:33:21.319 --> 01:33:23.697
humanity on an evolutionary scale.

01:33:24.155 --> 01:33:26.491
One has to adapt to survive.

01:33:29.828 --> 01:33:32.580
"That, changing like the
snake, I might be free

01:33:32.747 --> 01:33:36.376
to cast off flesh wherein
I dwell confined."

01:33:36.543 --> 01:33:40.879
Would you give it all up after
all you know, you can do?

01:33:41.006 --> 01:33:43.633
All the power you feel.

01:33:47.137 --> 01:33:49.555
I can save them.

01:33:56.187 --> 01:33:58.523
You won't get in the
way of my plan,

01:33:58.690 --> 01:34:00.317
Peter Parker.

01:34:26.718 --> 01:34:27.969
Go. Go.

01:35:04.339 --> 01:35:06.341
Nowhere to hide, Peter.

01:35:23.900 --> 01:35:26.319
All these souls lost and alone.

01:35:26.486 --> 01:35:27.486
I can save them.

01:35:27.529 --> 01:35:29.155
I can cure them.

01:35:29.322 --> 01:35:32.074
There's no need to stop me Peter.

01:35:41.543 --> 01:35:43.628
You're not thinking straight, Doc.

01:35:47.340 --> 01:35:48.967
Stop this. This isn't you.

01:35:54.139 --> 01:35:55.139
Let's talk this out.

01:35:56.224 --> 01:35:57.224
Doc.

01:36:03.064 --> 01:36:04.107
Oh, boy.

01:36:09.696 --> 01:36:10.739
You don't want to talk?

01:36:11.573 --> 01:36:13.116
There you go.

01:36:16.745 --> 01:36:20.332
Don't make me

01:36:20.498 --> 01:36:23.000
have to hurt you.

01:36:30.842 --> 01:36:32.177
That is disgusting.

01:36:42.228 --> 01:36:43.605
Gwen.

01:37:07.545 --> 01:37:09.203
I'm gonna throw you
out the window.

01:37:09.204 --> 01:37:10.204
What?

01:37:22.978 --> 01:37:25.855
Somebody's been a bad lizard.

01:38:12.736 --> 01:38:14.821
This is Lieutenant Williams
from the New York City

01:38:14.988 --> 01:38:18.450
Police Department. We've got
this building surrounded.

01:38:27.625 --> 01:38:29.627
Alpha, let's move ahead. Go.

01:38:41.264 --> 01:38:42.557
- Hey.
- Where are you?

01:38:42.724 --> 01:38:43.724
I'm fine. I'm okay.

01:38:43.808 --> 01:38:45.634
I'm in the sewer,
tracking him. I gotta

01:38:45.635 --> 01:38:47.187
stop him before anyone gets hurt.

01:38:47.354 --> 01:38:48.480
But we need an antidote.

01:38:48.647 --> 01:38:51.232
- Do you know how to run a serum?
- I do it all the time.

01:38:51.399 --> 01:38:53.818
Okay, great. Okay, I need
you to go to Oscorp.

01:38:53.985 --> 01:38:56.544
I need you to access the
cross-species file.

01:38:56.545 --> 01:38:59.082
It's a blue serum. File: 12389.

01:38:59.449 --> 01:39:00.533
Okay, got it.

01:39:00.700 --> 01:39:02.452
On my way.

01:39:33.942 --> 01:39:35.756
I spent my life as
a scientist trying

01:39:35.757 --> 01:39:39.906
to create a world without
weakness, without outcasts.

01:39:40.073 --> 01:39:42.617
I sought to create a
stronger human being,

01:39:42.784 --> 01:39:44.703
but there's no such thing.

01:39:44.869 --> 01:39:49.958
Human beings are weak, pathetic,
feeble-minded creatures.

01:39:50.125 --> 01:39:54.004
Why be human at all when
we can be so much more?

01:39:54.170 --> 01:39:56.464
Faster. Stronger.

01:39:56.631 --> 01:39:58.049
Smarter.

01:39:58.216 --> 01:40:01.052
This is my gift to you.

01:40:09.561 --> 01:40:11.229
Oscorp.

01:40:13.481 --> 01:40:14.607
- Captain Stacy.
- What?

01:40:14.774 --> 01:40:17.235
We have a confirmed sighting,
sir. The Lizard's headed

01:40:17.402 --> 01:40:19.612
- toward Canal Street.
- What about Spider-Man?

01:40:19.779 --> 01:40:20.989
Inside the high school.

01:40:21.156 --> 01:40:23.074
I want that Spider-Man
off the street.

01:42:09.681 --> 01:42:12.559
The lizard creature has
released a biological agent.

01:42:12.726 --> 01:42:14.519
All efforts to stop
him have failed

01:42:14.686 --> 01:42:17.897
and he is now proceeding
north on 7th Avenue. Over.

01:42:21.901 --> 01:42:22.901
- Hi.
- Where are you?

01:42:22.944 --> 01:42:24.237
Peter, hi. I'm at Oscorp.

01:42:24.404 --> 01:42:26.156
You have to get out of there now.

01:42:26.323 --> 01:42:28.700
- The antidote is cooking.
- No, no, no.

01:42:28.867 --> 01:42:31.328
Connors is on the way. He's
coming to you right now.

01:42:31.494 --> 01:42:34.039
He needs the device. He's
gonna infect the whole city.

01:42:34.205 --> 01:42:35.373
Eight minutes left.

01:42:35.540 --> 01:42:38.084
You're gonna wait eight minutes
after what I told you?

01:42:38.251 --> 01:42:39.586
You leave right now.

01:42:39.753 --> 01:42:40.795
That is an order, okay?

01:42:40.962 --> 01:42:42.047
I'll get everybody out.

01:42:42.213 --> 01:42:43.715
Did you hear what?

01:42:43.882 --> 01:42:46.926
Gwen. Gwen. You Mother
Hubbard. Are you serious?

01:43:03.443 --> 01:43:04.611
He's heading south.

01:43:15.372 --> 01:43:17.374
Stand down now, or
we will open fire.

01:43:17.540 --> 01:43:20.794
You are surrounded.
There is no escape.

01:43:21.252 --> 01:43:22.671
Go, go.

01:44:24.607 --> 01:44:25.984
Clear.

01:44:26.151 --> 01:44:27.277
Clear up top.

01:44:29.112 --> 01:44:30.363
Clear, sir.

01:44:30.530 --> 01:44:31.698
All clear here, sir.

01:44:57.182 --> 01:44:58.725
Freeze.

01:44:59.392 --> 01:45:00.560
Down on the ground.

01:45:00.727 --> 01:45:02.187
Your hands behind your head.

01:45:02.354 --> 01:45:03.980
Now.

01:45:07.359 --> 01:45:08.818
Parker.

01:45:10.695 --> 01:45:11.696
It's headed to Oscorp.

01:45:11.863 --> 01:45:14.240
And your daughter's
there right now.

01:45:27.003 --> 01:45:28.296
You gotta let me go.

01:45:42.894 --> 01:45:43.894
Hold your fire.

01:45:50.735 --> 01:45:53.238
Well, Paul, if I didn't see
it, I wouldn't believe it.

01:45:53.405 --> 01:45:55.824
I won't venture to say
what it is crawling up

01:45:55.991 --> 01:45:57.909
the north side of
the Oscorp Tower,

01:45:58.076 --> 01:46:01.329
but clearly it is not human
and it is very, very strong.

01:46:17.637 --> 01:46:19.639
Time remaining: one minute.

01:47:32.587 --> 01:47:34.673
Antidote complete.

01:47:47.519 --> 01:47:49.229
Oh, man.

01:47:49.396 --> 01:47:52.065
We're getting the latest
details. This is just coming in.

01:47:52.232 --> 01:47:53.900
The New York Police Department

01:47:54.067 --> 01:47:56.069
has called for a
city-wide evacuation,

01:47:56.236 --> 01:47:58.196
everything south of 54th Street.

01:47:59.030 --> 01:48:00.824
If you are south of 54th Street,

01:48:00.991 --> 01:48:03.451
you have to move out of
the area immediately.

01:48:12.919 --> 01:48:15.505
Spider-Man appears to be
heading towards Oscorp.

01:48:15.672 --> 01:48:16.715
He looks injured

01:48:16.881 --> 01:48:19.551
and it's really not clear
if he's gonna make it.

01:48:19.718 --> 01:48:22.345
That's the guy who saved
my boy on the bridge.

01:48:22.512 --> 01:48:23.888
Troy, they're clearing us out.

01:48:24.055 --> 01:48:26.474
Something bad's going
down in Midtown.

01:48:26.641 --> 01:48:29.227
Still friends with Matthews,
that crane operator on 6th?

01:48:29.394 --> 01:48:31.313
- Yeah.
- Get him on the phone for me.

01:48:31.479 --> 01:48:33.565
The cops are evacuating everybody.

01:48:33.732 --> 01:48:35.942
Get him on the phone for me.

01:48:53.543 --> 01:48:56.171
Hey, Charlie, get me
Enrique: on 54th Street.

01:48:56.338 --> 01:48:58.423
- You got it.
- Angelo, get your mug over here.

01:48:58.590 --> 01:49:00.925
Wolski. You're getting
some overtime.

01:49:02.302 --> 01:49:04.262
All tower cranes on 6th,

01:49:04.429 --> 01:49:08.141
swing your jib arms over the
avenue Boom angles at 90 degrees.

01:49:08.308 --> 01:49:10.644
Spider-Man needs those big
boys high and lined up.

01:49:10.810 --> 01:49:12.854
Let's give him a clear
approach. Over.

01:49:46.596 --> 01:49:48.264
Come on, Parker.

01:51:44.005 --> 01:51:45.005
Hey.

01:51:45.006 --> 01:51:46.091
Dad.

01:51:46.257 --> 01:51:47.784
I have to get this to Spider-Man.

01:51:47.785 --> 01:51:48.785
Get in.

01:51:48.786 --> 01:51:50.428
- It can stop the Lizard.
- Get in the car.

01:51:50.595 --> 01:51:53.473
- You don't understand.
- Yes, I do.

01:51:53.640 --> 01:51:55.892
Your boyfriend is a
man of many masks.

01:51:56.059 --> 01:51:57.227
I get it.

01:51:57.394 --> 01:52:00.480
Give me this. Get in the car.

01:52:04.067 --> 01:52:06.152
Please make sure he's okay.

01:52:18.665 --> 01:52:21.668
Initialising Ganali device.

01:52:21.835 --> 01:52:24.838
Detonation in T-minus two minutes.

01:53:47.128 --> 01:53:49.673
Poor Peter Parker.

01:53:50.799 --> 01:53:57.472
No mother, no father, no uncle.

01:53:58.640 --> 01:54:00.517
All alone.

01:54:01.768 --> 01:54:02.769
He's not alone.

01:54:21.830 --> 01:54:24.416
Detonation in T-minus 45 seconds.

01:54:33.258 --> 01:54:34.258
Hey.

01:54:34.259 --> 01:54:35.259
Gift from Gwen.

01:54:37.512 --> 01:54:38.972
I got this, Peter. Go.

01:54:44.894 --> 01:54:47.981
T-minus 30 seconds.

01:55:05.749 --> 01:55:09.085
Detonation in T-minus 10 seconds.

01:55:09.544 --> 01:55:10.544
Nine.

01:55:11.755 --> 01:55:12.755
Eight.

01:55:13.465 --> 01:55:14.465
Seven.

01:55:15.342 --> 01:55:16.342
Six.

01:55:17.427 --> 01:55:18.427
Five.

01:55:19.429 --> 01:55:20.429
Four.

01:55:21.097 --> 01:55:22.097
Three.

01:55:23.850 --> 01:55:24.850
Two.

01:55:26.269 --> 01:55:27.269
One.

01:55:52.712 --> 01:55:54.212
No.

01:55:55.882 --> 01:55:57.382
No.

01:57:08.955 --> 01:57:10.081
The Captain.

01:57:11.624 --> 01:57:13.126
Captain.

01:57:15.795 --> 01:57:17.179
The Lizard.

01:57:17.180 --> 01:57:18.180
It's okay.

01:57:18.256 --> 01:57:19.466
We stopped him.

01:57:20.133 --> 01:57:21.133
Okay.

01:57:21.176 --> 01:57:23.345
Let's get you out
of here. Come on.

01:57:24.679 --> 01:57:26.014
Okay, okay, okay.

01:57:26.181 --> 01:57:27.641
Look at me. Stay with me.

01:57:27.807 --> 01:57:29.893
- Help's on the way, okay?
- You need to...

01:57:30.060 --> 01:57:33.563
You need to be gone
when they get here.

01:57:33.730 --> 01:57:35.065
Okay?

01:57:35.231 --> 01:57:36.524
I'm not going anywhere.

01:57:37.108 --> 01:57:39.527
I was wrong about you, Peter.

01:57:40.236 --> 01:57:41.780
This city needs you.

01:57:43.782 --> 01:57:45.367
Here.

01:57:45.533 --> 01:57:46.701
You're gonna need this.

01:57:51.122 --> 01:57:53.083
You're gonna make enemies.

01:57:55.502 --> 01:57:57.337
People will get hurt.

01:57:58.922 --> 01:58:00.840
Sometimes the people
closest to you.

01:58:04.761 --> 01:58:06.763
So I want you to promise
me something, okay?

01:58:08.682 --> 01:58:12.477
Leave Gwen out of it.

01:58:15.021 --> 01:58:16.648
Promise me that.

01:58:22.278 --> 01:58:23.947
You promise me.

01:59:37.646 --> 01:59:41.107
An eerie calm has set
in over New York City.

01:59:41.274 --> 01:59:42.567
Apparently, some sort of

01:59:42.734 --> 01:59:45.737
aerosolised antidote
was launched from

01:59:45.904 --> 01:59:49.115
Oscorp Tower, which seems to
have counteracted the biotoxins.

01:59:49.282 --> 01:59:52.243
Residents of Lower Manhattan
can rest peacefully,

01:59:52.410 --> 01:59:54.412
knowing that the
alleged mastermind,

01:59:54.579 --> 01:59:58.208
of this terror plot, Dr Curtis
Connors, is behind bars.

01:59:58.375 --> 01:59:59.751
We've got John Niles,

01:59:59.918 --> 02:00:02.337
on the street for a report
in Lower Manhattan.

02:00:02.504 --> 02:00:04.547
John, what do you see?

02:00:37.414 --> 02:00:39.457
Sweetheart, it's all right.

02:00:41.626 --> 02:00:43.503
It's all right.

02:00:44.587 --> 02:00:46.006
It's all right.

02:00:46.506 --> 02:00:47.506
Rough night.

02:00:49.551 --> 02:00:51.219
It's gonna be all right.

02:01:44.981 --> 02:01:46.691
Where have you been?

02:01:49.694 --> 02:01:51.279
Hi.

02:01:56.117 --> 02:01:57.744
My father died.

02:02:01.706 --> 02:02:03.458
There was a funeral.

02:02:04.918 --> 02:02:11.007
They shot off rifles and
they made speeches.

02:02:14.552 --> 02:02:16.513
Two of my teachers showed up.

02:02:17.931 --> 02:02:19.307
And Flash showed up.

02:02:24.229 --> 02:02:26.856
Everyone was there but you.

02:02:41.454 --> 02:02:43.581
Can't do this. Can't do this.

02:02:45.834 --> 02:02:47.877
I'm sorry. I can't...

02:02:48.044 --> 02:02:49.462
What are you saying?

02:02:49.629 --> 02:02:51.464
I can't see you any more.

02:02:53.425 --> 02:02:54.884
I can't.

02:03:20.493 --> 02:03:22.495
He made you promise, didn't he?

02:03:26.499 --> 02:03:30.378
To stay away from
me, so I'd be safe.

02:03:56.863 --> 02:03:58.864
What a pretty girl.

02:03:58.907 --> 02:04:00.075
Yeah.

02:04:00.241 --> 02:04:02.035
That's what Uncle Ben said.

02:04:03.078 --> 02:04:04.746
Did you ask her out?

02:04:08.500 --> 02:04:09.834
Why?

02:04:10.919 --> 02:04:12.379
Can't.

02:04:13.672 --> 02:04:15.048
Why?

02:04:17.634 --> 02:04:19.344
I'm just no good for her.

02:04:22.514 --> 02:04:25.976
Peter Parker, if there's one
thing you are, it's good.

02:04:27.018 --> 02:04:30.063
Anyone has a problem with
that can talk to me.

02:04:47.789 --> 02:04:50.834
Peter, I know things have been

02:04:51.001 --> 02:04:54.462
difficult lately and
I'm sorry about that.

02:04:54.879 --> 02:04:57.841
I think I know what
you're feeling.

02:04:58.008 --> 02:05:00.593
Ever since you were a little boy,

02:05:00.760 --> 02:05:05.181
you've been living with so
many unresolved things.

02:05:06.391 --> 02:05:08.685
Well, take it from an old man:

02:05:09.269 --> 02:05:12.355
Those things send us down a road.

02:05:12.522 --> 02:05:14.858
They make us who we are.

02:05:15.108 --> 02:05:20.363
And if anyone's destined for
greatness, it's you, son.

02:05:20.947 --> 02:05:23.366
You owe the world your gifts.

02:05:23.950 --> 02:05:26.828
You just have to figure
out how to use them.

02:05:27.370 --> 02:05:33.168
And know that wherever they
take you, we'll always be here.

02:05:34.002 --> 02:05:36.588
So come on home, Peter.

02:05:37.464 --> 02:05:39.299
You're my hero.

02:05:39.466 --> 02:05:40.967
And I love you.

02:05:49.392 --> 02:05:51.102
- What's up, Parker?
- What's up?

02:05:51.269 --> 02:05:52.729
Hey. How's it going?

02:05:53.688 --> 02:05:55.065
You coming along, man?

02:05:56.650 --> 02:05:57.650
Cool shirt.

02:05:59.361 --> 02:06:00.487
Yeah.

02:06:00.654 --> 02:06:02.155
Dude's crazy.

02:06:02.322 --> 02:06:03.698
But chicks dig him.

02:06:06.493 --> 02:06:09.204
Come on, guys, you heard
the bell. Get to class.

02:06:18.672 --> 02:06:21.549
I had a professor once who
liked to tell his students,

02:06:21.716 --> 02:06:24.970
that there were only 10 different
plots in all of fiction.

02:06:25.929 --> 02:06:28.014
Well, I'm here to tell
you he was wrong.

02:06:28.181 --> 02:06:29.599
There is only one:

02:06:30.517 --> 02:06:32.018
"Who am I"?

02:06:32.727 --> 02:06:34.646
Mr Parker.

02:06:34.813 --> 02:06:35.814
Tardy again.

02:06:37.774 --> 02:06:39.609
At least we can
always count on you.

02:06:39.776 --> 02:06:42.529
Sorry, Miss Ritter, won't
happen again, I promise.

02:06:42.696 --> 02:06:44.781
Don't make promises
you can't keep.

02:06:47.033 --> 02:06:49.202
Yeah, but those are the best kind.

02:06:49.369 --> 02:06:51.204
Okay, class, open your books.

02:06:51.371 --> 02:06:53.373
Let's begin on page one.

02:09:48.631 --> 02:09:51.217
Hello, doctor.

02:09:51.384 --> 02:09:52.719
Did you tell the boy?

02:09:52.886 --> 02:09:53.928
Tell him what?

02:09:54.095 --> 02:09:57.849
Did you tell the boy the
truth about his father?

02:09:59.517 --> 02:10:00.517
No.

02:10:00.560 --> 02:10:02.145
Well, that's very good.

02:10:02.479 --> 02:10:04.730
So we'll let him be for now.

02:10:05.732 --> 02:10:07.817
You should leave him alone.
